# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# CLERK AUTHENTICATION
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Get these from: https://dashboard.clerk.com/apps/[your-app]/api-keys
# The trailing `# @required` marker is the SINGLE machine-readable source for
# the first-run contract: lib/env/requiredEnv.ts parses these lines, never a
# hand-typed list (see .claude/rules/derive-never-type.md). Comment-only — it
# changes no value.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX  # @required
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX  # @required

# Sign-in/Sign-up URLs — consumed by the Clerk SDK / <ClerkProvider> by naming
# convention (not read via process.env in app code). Keep the NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_*
# names exactly; Clerk resolves them itself.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL=/sign-in
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_URL=/sign-up

# After sign-in/up redirects — also Clerk-convention vars (optional; Clerk
# defaults to / when unset).
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_AFTER_SIGN_IN_URL=/dashboard
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_AFTER_SIGN_UP_URL=/guided/step-1

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# CLERK JWT ISSUER (for Convex integration)
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Get this from: Clerk Dashboard → JWT Templates → convex template → Issuer
# ⚠️ IMPORTANT: Domain only, WITHOUT https://
# ✅ Correct: your-app.clerk.accounts.dev
# ❌ Wrong: https://your-app.clerk.accounts.dev
CLERK_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN=your-app.clerk.accounts.dev  # @required

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# CLERK CUSTOM DOMAIN (for the Content-Security-Policy)
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Your Clerk custom/satellite domain, added to script-src and frame-src in the CSP
# (see lib/csp.mjs, shared by middleware.ts and next.config.mjs).
# LEAVE THIS UNSET if you use Clerk's development domain — https://*.clerk.accounts.dev
# is always allowed, so a fork works out of the box with no value here.
# Only set it once you configure a Clerk custom domain in production.
# Accepted with or without https:// — e.g. clerk.your-domain.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_DOMAIN=  # @required

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# CONVEX BACKEND
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Get these after running: npx convex dev
# ⚠️ IMPORTANT: Both URLs must be identical and include https://

# For prebuild script (Vercel deployment)
CONVEX_URL=https://your-project.convex.cloud

# For client-side connection
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=https://your-project.convex.cloud  # @required

# For Vercel prebuild — consumed by the Convex CLI / `convex deploy` during the
# Vercel build (scripts/check-production-env.mjs asserts it names the same
# deployment slug as NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL). Not read by app source code.
# Same value as NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL.
CONVEX_URL=https://your-project.convex.cloud

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# APPLICATION URLS
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Canonical site origin for metadataBase / robots / sitemap.
# Read by: app/layout.tsx, app/robots.ts, app/sitemap.ts (+ a11y pages).
# Optional — falls back to https://vantagestarter.ai, but set it in production
# so canonical URLs, robots and the sitemap point at your real domain.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com

# Allowed CORS origin for the orchestration HTTP endpoints.
# Read by: convex/http/orchestration.ts (Access-Control-Allow-Origin).
# Optional — falls back to https://vantagestarter.com. Set it to your app
# origin if you call the orchestration HTTP API cross-origin.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://your-domain.com

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# BILLING (Polar.sh)
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Polar product IDs mapped to the three subscription tiers.
# Read by: convex/polar.ts (products.tier_1/2/3).
# Optional to boot (fall back to ""), but required for checkout to resolve a
# product. Get from: https://polar.sh dashboard → Products.
POLAR_PRODUCT_TIER_1=
POLAR_PRODUCT_TIER_2=
POLAR_PRODUCT_TIER_3=

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# AI SERVICES
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# OpenAI API — translation script + Convex RAG embeddings.
# Read by: scripts/translate.js and convex/lib/rag.ts (via @ai-sdk/openai,
# which reads OPENAI_API_KEY automatically).
# Get from: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

# Firecrawl API — web scraping for the ingestion pipeline.
# Read by: convex/lib/firecrawl.ts (throws FirecrawlKeyMissingError when unset).
# Optional — only required if you use the scrape feature.
# Get from: https://firecrawl.dev
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=fc-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

# Together.ai API — NOT read by shipped code. Runtime AI routes through
# @ai-sdk/gateway (AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY, see lib/ai/providers.ts). Kept as an
# optional direct-provider key for forks that wire Together directly.
# Declared divergence: documented but not read by the shipped socle.
# TOGETHER_API_KEY=XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

# fal.ai API — NOT read by shipped code (same reason as TOGETHER_API_KEY:
# AI goes through @ai-sdk/gateway). Kept as an optional direct-provider key.
# Declared divergence: documented but not read by the shipped socle.
# Format: key_id:key_secret — get from: https://fal.ai/dashboard/keys
# FAL_KEY=XXXXXXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXXXXXXXXXX:XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# ORCHESTRATION (issue report → task integration)
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Where in-app issue reports are forwarded as tasks.
# Read by: convex/issueReports.ts (both must be set, or the report is validated
# but returns configured:false — a fresh fork works out of the box unset).
# Optional — leave unset unless you wire the peer task endpoint.
VANTAGE_PEERS_TASK_URL=
VANTAGE_PEERS_API_KEY=

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# RESEND (Transactional Email)
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Get from: https://resend.com/api-keys
# Must be set in Convex dashboard too (npx convex env set RESEND_API_KEY re_xxx)
RESEND_API_KEY=re_XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# E2E TESTING
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# Browserbase — optional; e2e tests run locally without these.
# When set, Playwright connects to Browserbase cloud browsers via WebSocket
# instead of launching a local Chromium. Get from: https://browserbase.com
BROWSERBASE_API_KEY=
BROWSERBASE_PROJECT_ID=

# Clerk Testing Mode — OTP bypass for e2e authenticated tests.
# Generate from: Clerk Dashboard → Testing → Testing tokens
# Tests skip automatically when this is absent.
CLERK_TESTING_TOKEN=

# Base URL for Playwright tests (defaults to http://localhost:3000)
PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
